Building Python 3.14 for RISC OS
================================

Python is cross compiled on Linux with the GCC 16 RISC OS cross compiler
(arm-riscos-gnueabihf-gcc, https://github.com/robheaton/riscos-gcc16).
The RISC OS build uses hand maintained versions of the files that configure
would normally generate:

  RISCOS/pyconfig.h   - generated by RISCOS/mkpyconfig.py
  RISCOS/Makefile     - generated by RISCOS/mkmakefile.py
  RISCOS/config.c     - the table of built-in modules (Modules/config.c)
  RISCOS/getpath.c    - replaces Modules/getpath.c and Modules/getpath.py

and these RISC OS specific sources:

  RISCOS/swimodule.c  - the swi module
  Lib/riscospath.py   - os.path for RISC OS


1. A build Python
-----------------

The build needs a Python 3.14 for the build machine (the same version,
since it is used to freeze modules and run the code generators).  Build it
from a separate, clean checkout of the same source:

    git worktree add --detach ../cpython-build/src-3.14 python-314
    mkdir -p ../cpython-build/host && cd ../cpython-build/host
    ../src-3.14/configure --prefix=$PWD/../host-install
    make -j8 && make install

(ensurepip may fail if zlib is not installed on the build machine; the
interpreter itself is still installed.)


2. Cross compile
----------------

From the top of the source tree:

    export PATH=<toolchain>/bin:$PATH
    make -f RISCOS/Makefile BUILD_PYTHON=<build python> -j8

This builds:

    python                       the interpreter (an ELF executable)
    Modules/*.cpython-314-arm-riscos.so
                                 shared extension modules
    build/lib.riscos-arm-3.14/   links to the shared extension modules
    pybuilddir.txt               tells the interpreter where they are

Variables that can be set on the make command line:

    CROSS_PREFIX      compiler prefix (default arm-riscos-gnueabihf-)
    BUILD_PYTHON      the build Python (default python3.14)
    TOOLCHAIN_LIBDIR  where libdl is (default <toolchain>/lib)

Modules are not built if their libraries are missing: zlib, _ssl, _hashlib,
_ctypes (libffi), _bz2, _lzma, _sqlite3, _zstd, readline, _curses, _dbm,
_gdbm, _uuid and _tkinter.  resource is disabled (UnixLib's
<sys/resource.h> is incomplete).


3. Running on RISC OS
---------------------

The executable needs the runtime libraries from the toolchain release,
installed with PackMan: SharedLibs-C-armeabihf.

The build tree can be used in place.  When it is copied to RISC OS (for
example over a network share, where '.' and '/' are swapped in names),
set the type of the executable to ELF:

    *SetType python ELF

and run it from the top of the tree.  It finds the standard library in
<dir>.Lib and the shared modules using pybuilddir/txt.  Files in Lib keep
their /py suffix, which the RISC OS import system accepts.

When installed in !Python3 the layout is:

    !Python3.Bin.python314              the executable
    !Python3.Python314.Lib              the standard library
    !Python3.Python314.Lib.lib-dynload  shared extension modules


4. Updating to a new Python version
-----------------------------------

Run configure in cross compile mode against the UnixLib headers, using a
separate build directory:

    mkdir ../cpython-build/cross-probe && cd ../cpython-build/cross-probe
    CONFIG_SITE=<src>/RISCOS/config.site \
    CC=arm-riscos-gnueabihf-gcc CXX=arm-riscos-gnueabihf-g++ \
    AR=arm-riscos-gnueabihf-ar READELF=arm-riscos-gnueabihf-readelf \
    LDFLAGS=-L<toolchain>/lib \
      <clean src>/configure --host=arm-linux-gnueabihf \
        --build=x86_64-pc-linux-gnu --with-build-python=<build python> \
        --without-mimalloc --disable-ipv6 --without-ensurepip --prefix=/Python3

(configure only accepts known cross compile hosts, so arm-linux-gnueabihf is
used with the RISC OS compiler.  The results are fixed up by the scripts.)

Then regenerate the hand maintained files:

    python3 RISCOS/mkpyconfig.py ../cpython-build/cross-probe/pyconfig.h RISCOS/pyconfig.h
    python3 RISCOS/mkmakefile.py ../cpython-build/cross-probe/Makefile RISCOS/Makefile

and update RISCOS/config.c from Modules/Setup.bootstrap.in (the built-in
modules) and Modules/config.c.in.
